\chapter{Multikernel Partitioning and Subsystem Personalities}

\section{Barrelfish Partitioning and Framekernel TCB}

At the macro scale, hardware is split into independent microkernel nodes following the Barrelfish multikernel architecture \footcite{baum09}. Within each node, shared memory and memory safety are maintained using an Asterinas-style Framekernel written in Rust \footcite{peng24}, isolating hardware drivers and memory operations inside explicit safety domains.

\section{Dynamic Personality Redirection}

To support foreign operating system Binaries (such as Linux ELF or Windows PE executables), Telix incorporates dynamic system call redirection tables \footcite{gerb01}. Foreign OS ABIs run atop user-level microkernel applications \footcite{golu91} backed by distributed Mach-style cluster messaging \footcite{zajc93, rash87, milo93}.
